<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Epson models that collect waste ink in a user-replaceable maintenance box or
  tank instead of an internal absorbent pad.

  WHY THIS LIST EXISTS

  On these models the fill level is kept on the box's own chip, so the printer
  holds no counter for this app to reset. That makes them permanently
  unsupported for counter resets, which is a different situation from a model
  that is merely missing from devices.xml and could still be added.

  The catalog cannot work this out on its own. Three candidate signals were
  measured against a known classification and all three failed:

    the printer class attribute, identical ("epson.printer.dd4.standard")
      across maintenance-box models and models absent from the database
    the EPxx spec, mixed (EP10: 56 without a box, 112 with one)
    the presence of a waste node, absent in 275 of the 276 affected models
      and split 159 / 116 between the two causes

  So the distinction has to be carried as data.

  COVERAGE

  This file is a seed, not a complete list. Epson has shipped maintenance boxes
  across hundreds of models, including consumer ones. A model missing here is
  not mislabelled: it falls back to the neutral explanation, which names both
  possible causes rather than guessing. Adding entries only ever makes the
  message more specific.

  PROVENANCE

  Every entry records where the claim came from, so it can be re-checked against
  Epson later. Only Epson's own pages are used as sources here: a claim taken
  from a retailer listing is only as good as that retailer.

  NOTE: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, so no dash underlines.
-->
<maintenanceBoxes>

    <!-- Source: epson.com.au product page 12267, which names the compatible
         printers for this tank verbatim. -->
    <box part="C12C934591" source="https://www.epson.com.au/products/options-accessories/12267">
        <model>ET-8550</model>
        <model>ET-8500</model>
        <model>ET-5800</model>
        <model>ET-16600</model>
        <model>WF-7830</model>
        <model>WF-7840</model>
        <model>WF-7845</model>
        <model>D560</model>
    </box>

</maintenanceBoxes>
